Z||000000||camon||11-12-2001||01:55 AM||||I have a question regarding what you guys use for windshild washer fluid?<P>The reason I ask is because the stuff i'm using when spayed from the washers slashes and manages to find it's way to the rear sail panel windows of my 87 GT and I just noticed today that I have these little tiny cracks forming at the front edge of the sail panel plastic. I believe the washer fluid is doing it because  after using the washers I seen some washer fluid on the door windows and on the sail panels!<P>------------------<BR>Keith||||reg||1
Z||000001||Nashco||11-12-2001||02:29 AM||||If it's taken this long for your windows to start cracking, consider yourself gifted.  A LOT of the plastic quarter windows are bad, which is why there are aftermarket replacements available.  Mine are well beyond cracking, and I highly doubt the windshield washer fluid had anything to do with it.  I don't think the previous owner even used the squirters..since he had lost the cap and the bottle was obviously not used for a long time!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||11-12-2001||09:12 AM||||Wish I could get my washers to work.  It's something electrical, but I can't figure out where the wiring leads to.  I'd hate to have to add a wire.  So cheap, but that may be my only alternative.  I'd like to use the switch on the stalk (actually steering column).  Anyone have any suggestions?||||reg||1
Z||000003||BC-GT||11-12-2001||11:37 AM||||Hey Monkeyman, try this link from the Ogre's cave. Has the best logical info I've seen yet. I had the same trouble as you, just went out with this info yesterday and at least got my pump to squirt once through the column switch. <A HREF="http://home.t-online.de/home/O_Scholz/fieroidx.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.t-online.de/home/O_Scholz/fieroidx.html</A> <BR>It's in the trobleshooting section under "delay wipers"<P>------------------<BR>Darryl Martin<BR>1985 GT <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.imagestation.com/picture/pf251a969c96964ef15691e97e7ac4489/feb64e3a.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
